utive Order No.  \n7968, as amended; 22 CFR 103.1), is  \namended by deleting therefrom Items  \nNo. 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5.\nAll prior Executive orders inconsistent  \nherewith are amended accordingly.\nThis order shall become effective ten  \ndays after the date of its publidafton in  \nthe F e d e r a l R e g is t e r. x\nD w i g h t D . E is e n h o w e r\nT h e W h it e H o u s e,\nOctober 10, 1955.\n[F . R . Doc. 55-8415; F iled , Oct. 13, 1955;\n12:00 m .]","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-10639-8a69a85b7a.txt","sha256":"51f4573a519b8ae8150169f4b213ab44e6a06353308f7a0bef468498233e9a32","source":{"line":1791,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"2648147bf3d46ce08236ed2094c263def0f426ed09cf4e7b6cdf8cc48f1f125b"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:10639\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1955-10-14/pdf/FR-1955-10-14.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 8a69a85b7a9354e915002554a21819dd39c9dddf13f70d57ef50f97b0c180de4\nLocation: 20 FR 7717, PDF pages 1-15 (confidence medium)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 50 ===\n^ xO N A M / ? (\nFEDERALREGISTER\nXV '  HUjJ-r ^\nVOLUME 20 ^ / , 1934\n*  O N l T l O *\nNUMBER 201\nWashingtont Friday, October 14, 1955\nT U tE 3 — TH E PRESID EN T \nPROCLAMATION 3115 \nColumbus  D a y, 1955 \nBY THE PRESIDENT OP THE UNITED STATES \nOF AMERICA \nA PROCLAMATION\nWHEREAS Christopher Columbus,  \nwith a fleet of three vessels, daringly  \nset sail upon an unknown sea and per­\nsevered until he landed upon a strange  \nshore, thus discovering a new continent  \nand a new world; and  \nWHEREAS appropriate recognition  \nshould be given to the memory of this  \ngreat navigator, whose exploits have in­\nspired other brave men throughout the  \ncenturies to seek those opportunities  \nwhich lie beyond the horizon; and  \nWHEREAS October 12, 1492, the date  \nof the sighting of land by Columbus’ in­\ntrepid crew, marks the beginning of a  \nnew epoch in mankind’s ever-widening  \nsearch for a freer and a richer life; and  \nWHEREAS a grateful Congress, in ap­\npreciation of the debt we owe to  \nChristop","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10639.txt","sha256":"00b3de418af9276d9db3856eb12b5ad35fee54822bfabb00fd458420cb100815","source":{"line":843,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"59c6c901f59185f1271a516dae484f50b0bf7a975834e2273d7d79faf17ee8bb"}}]}
